   "evidence": "mathlib/Mathlib/RingTheory/Spectrum/Prime/Topology.lean:1323 `theorem specializes_closedPoint (x : PrimeSpectrum R) : x \u2933 closedPoint R`. Mathlib proves `closedPoint_mem_iff` itself at line 1330 with `(specializes_closedPoint x).mem_open U.2 h`, so the direct route already exists.",
   "file": "TauCeti/RingTheory/LocalRing/Spectrum.lean",
   "fix": "Replace `htop`, `hmem` and the `rw [htop]; trivial` block with `have heq : (\u27e8p, hp\u27e9 : PrimeSpectrum R) = closedPoint R := (specializes_closedPoint _).mem_open h rfl` (or with `Set.mem_singleton_iff.mp` applied to that result). Then drop the `Opens` construction entirely.",
   "issue": "Lines 46\u201358 package `{closedPoint R}` as an `Opens`, prove it equals `\u22a4` via `closedPoint_mem_iff`, then rewrite with `rw [htop]; trivial`. Lines 52\u201358 then close `_ \u2208 {closedPoint R}` with `exact hmem`, where `hmem` is membership in the `Opens` structure. That step depends on undocumented defeq across the `Opens`/`SetLike` coercion, and the detour hides why the proof works: every point specializes to the closed point.",
   "line": 46
  }
 ],
